egs a and b, r=(a+b-h)/2, so the semiperimeter is s=h+r. The triangle area is rs=r(h+r), giving πr²/[r(h+r)]=πr/(h+r).","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_264"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1979_AMC_12_Q21","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_262","cnm_p148","cnm_p192"],"id":"tangent-lengths","label":"Use equal tangent lengths","methodDirectNodeIds":{"tangent-lengths":["cnm_264","math:triangle-area-radius-relations","cnm_263"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_264","math:triangle-area-radius-relations","cnm_263","cnm_262","cnm_p148","cnm_p192"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p148","cnm_p192","cnm_147"],"id":"area-pythagorean","label":"Combine area with the Pythagorean theorem","methodDirectNodeIds":{"area-pythagorean":["cnm_264","math:triangle-area-radius-relations","cnm_174"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_264","math:triangle-area-radius-relations","cnm_174","cnm_p148","cnm_p192","cnm_147"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:a1e4a1864ccdf7ab60e1c3e6"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E. 7/2","reason":"Set C=(0,0), A=(12,0), and B=(0,5). Then O=(6,5/2), I=(2,2), and R=13/2. Write M=(r,r), with 0<r≤5 because tangency is to the leg segments. Internal tangency gives (r−6)^2+(r−5/2)^2=(13/2−r)^2, yielding r=4; external tangency would give r=30, which is inadmissible. In the bounding rectangle [2,6]×[2,4], subtracting the three corner triangles gives [MOI]=8−2−3/2−1=7/2.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_264"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2018_AMC_12B_Q21","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"coordinate-circle-tangency","label":"Locate the centers using coordinates","methodDirectNodeIds":{"coordinate-circle-tangency":["cnm_264","cnm_265","cnm_h181","cnm_h173","math:triangle-area-radius-relations","math:shoelace-formula"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_264","cnm_265","cnm_h181","cnm_h173"